    {
      "title": "Samson defends bowlers after WI loss, says Tilak's wicket proved costly",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/samson-defends-bowlers-after-wi-loss-says-tilak-s-wicket-proved-costly-126101500188_1.html",
      "description": "Sanju Samson on Wednesday defended India's bowlers after their 24-run defeat to the West Indies in the fourth T20, saying the emerging pacers will improve with experience while identifying Tilak Varma's dismissal as the turning point of their failed chase.\nIndia were bowled out for 223 in 19.3 overs after the West Indies posted 247 for three, with Shai Hope smashing an unbeaten 102 off 50 balls and Keemo Paul claiming a five-wicket haul to level the five-match series at 2-2.\nSamson said India has no replacement for the rested Jasprit Bumrah, describing the pace spearhead as a once-in-a-generation bowler, but backed the emerging fast bowlers to improve with experience and opportunities.\n\"He is a once-in-a-generation bowler, and we are very lucky to have him. But we also have some really good talent coming through. Arshdeep has been doing a great job, and the way Prince Yadav has bowled in the last few games has been very impressive.\n\"We have some really good quality talent, and the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-15T06:11:27"
    },
    {
      "title": "Iyer stresses better execution and fresh mindset after T20I loss vs WI",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/iyer-stresses-better-execution-and-fresh-mindset-after-t20i-loss-vs-wi-126101500004_1.html",
      "description": "India skipper Shreyas Iyer on Wednesday stressed the need for better execution and the right mindset going forward after the hosts suffered a 24-run defeat against the West Indies in the fourth T20I here.\nIndia's innings ended at 223/9 in 19.3 overs after Arshdeep Singh retired hurt while chasing the West Indies' imposing total of 247 for three, allowing the visitors to level the five-match series 2-2.\nThe series decider will be played at the M Chinnaswamy Stadium in Bengaluru on Saturday.\n\"It all started with bowling. We didn't execute our line and lengths well and, at the end of the day, when you're chasing 250, you have to go about it in a certain pattern,\" Iyer said.\n\"I liked our approach during the chase, but we were unfortunate that we couldn't execute our plans with the ball, and that's where we fell a bit short.\"\n\"They executed their plans well, and there was a bit of assistance from the wicket as well. The ball was kicking up, and they used the field pretty well. So, cred",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-15T05:53:34"
    },
    {
      "title": "IND vs WI 4th T20I: Hope and Paul shine as West Indies level series 2-2",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/ind-vs-wi-4th-t20i-hope-and-paul-shine-as-west-indies-level-series-2-2-126101401391_1.html",
      "description": "Keemo Paul's 5 for 41 followed Shai Hope's first-innings 102 not out as a clinical West Indies beat India by 24 runs in the fourth T20I to level the five-match series 2-2 here on Wednesday.\nThe fifth and final T20I will be played on Saturday at Bengaluru's M Chinnaswamy Stadium.\nSanju Samson struck a 23-ball 56 at the top but India fell way short in the run chase, getting bowled out for 223 in reply to the West Indies' 247 for three.\nArshdeep Singh copped a blow to his right shoulder in the final over from Shamar Joseph and subsequently retired out.\nEarlier, Hope led the way with 102 not out as the West Indies posted a huge total. Hope struck nine sixes and four fours to make his runs off 50 balls.\nSherfane Rutherford made 49 not out off 26 balls with four fours and three sixes.\nBrief scores: West Indies 247/3 in 20 overs (Shai Hope 102 not out, Shimron Hetmyer 33, Sherfane Rutherford 49 not out; Prince Yadav 1/36) beat India 223 all out in 19.3 overs (Sanju Samson 56, Tilak Varm",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-15T05:01:16"
